# S18: Notes App

## Objective

Third dogfood app: `apps/notes` on port 3005. Markdown notes scoped to epics,
chats, or free-floating. Work-control Epics column gets a "targetApp: notes" option.
Accepting an epic in notes mode writes the plan to `apps/notes/planning/sprints/`.
Demonstrates that the orchestrator spine is truly app-agnostic.

## App

- Port: 3005
- Slug: `notes`
- Planning home: `apps/notes/planning/sprints/`

## Features

- Create / edit / delete markdown notes (CodeMirror or textarea)
- Link note to: epic ID, chat ID, or none
- Notes list: filter by linked scope
- Full-text search across notes
- Accept `targetApp: notes` in work-control epics column

## Tasks

- [ ] S18-T01-FreezeInvariants.pd
- [ ] S18-T02-AppScaffold.pd           — apps/notes Nuxt + planning instance
- [ ] S18-T03-NotesSchema.pd           — `notes_notes` table, repo interface
- [ ] S18-T04-CrudApi.pd               — /api/notes CRUD + defineFeatureHandler
- [ ] S18-T05-MarkdownEditor.pd        — editor UI + preview pane
- [ ] S18-T06-EpicLink.pd              — link note to epic/chat; back-link from board
- [ ] S18-T07-DevLauncher.pd           — `bun run dev:notes`, PORT_MAP 3005
- [ ] S18-T08-KnowledgeSlug.pd         — `notes.md` knowledge slug + company page
- [ ] S18-T09-TestsSmoke.pd

## Definition of Done

- [ ] `apps/notes` boots on :3005, CRUD notes persists
- [ ] Epic in work-control with `targetApp: notes` writes plan to notes/planning/
- [ ] Note linked to epic shows in board sidebar (back-link)
- [ ] `bun run feature:health` — `notes` slug green
- [ ] `bun run test` green

